  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Parosphromenus filamentosus is one of the larger Parosphromenus species and is known for the filament-like extension of its tail. It is relatively hardy, but like all Parosphromenus it requires live food. Males reach up to 3 cm.</p><p>Bronze body tones with dark red banding on the unpaired fins, followed by black banding with a rim of bright white or blue iridescence.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Occurs in Kalimantan Tengah (Borneo, Indonesia) in jungle river systems near Banjarmasin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Primarily inhabits peat swamp forests and associated blackwater streams.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<ul><li>Temperature: 22–28 °C</li><li>pH: 3.0–6.5</li><li>Hardness: 18–72 ppm</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>These fish are carnivorous and only consume live food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>These fish are generally peaceful and shy, preferring to hide among vegetation or other structures in their environment.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-linkei-1",
      "html": "<p>Conservation status: listed as Endangered by the IUCN due to habitat loss and degradation caused by deforestation, land use change and pollution.</p><p>Have the habitat ready before purchase.</p>"
    }
  ],
